MODULE 1: Introduction to Ethical Hacking
1. Cybersecurity kya hai?

Cybersecurity ka main purpose computer systems, networks, applications aur data ko unauthorized access, attack, damage ya theft se protect karna hai.

Simple example:
Agar college ka server hai, to usme students ka data hai. Cybersecurity ensure karegi ki koi unauthorized person us data ko access ya modify na kar sake.

2. Information Security kya hai?

Information Security (InfoSec) ka focus information/data ko protect karna hai.

Iska main goal hai:

Data private rahe
Data correct rahe
Data jab chahiye tab available rahe

Isi ko samajhne ke liye CIA Triad important hai.

3. CIA Triad ⭐

CIA = Confidentiality + Integrity + Availability

Confidentiality

Information sirf authorized person ko milni chahiye.

Example:
Tumhara password kisi aur ko nahi pata hona chahiye.

Integrity

Information unauthorized way mein change nahi honi chahiye.

Example:
College marksheet mein kisi ne tumhare marks secretly change kar diye → Integrity compromise.

Availability

Information/system jab authorized user ko chahiye, tab available hona chahiye.

Example:
Exam ke time college portal down ho gaya → Availability problem.

Yaad rakhna:

C = Secret
I = Correct
A = Available

4. CIA ke Additional Security Elements

Sir ke material mein CIA ke saath kuch additional elements bhi diye gaye hain.

Authentication

Tum kaun ho? ye verify karna.

Example: username + password.

Authorization

Tumhe kya karne ki permission hai?

Example: Student marks dekh sakta hai, lekin teacher marks modify kar sakta hai.

Non-Repudiation

Kisi action ko later deny na kiya ja sake.

Example: digitally signed transaction ka proof.

Accountability

System mein kisne kya action kiya, uska record maintain karna.

Risk Management

Possible risks ko identify karke unhe reduce/manage karna.

5. Data Security mein 3 Important Problems
Disclosure

Unauthorized person ko information mil jana.

Alteration

Data unauthorized way mein change ho jana.

Destruction

Data/system/application destroy ya inaccessible ho jana.

6. Cyber Kill Chain ⭐

Cyber Kill Chain ek framework hai jo explain karta hai ki attacker attack ko step-by-step kaise carry out karta hai.

Iske 7 stages hain:

1. Reconnaissance

Attacker target ke baare mein information collect karta hai.

Example:

IP
employees
network
systems
2. Weaponization

Collected information ke basis par attacker malicious payload/tool prepare karta hai.

3. Delivery

Payload target tak pahunchaya jata hai.

Example:

Email
Malicious link
USB
Vulnerable application
4. Exploitation

Attacker vulnerability exploit karke system mein entry lene ki attempt karta hai.

5. Installation

Malicious software/payload install karke access maintain karne ki attempt hoti hai.

6. Command & Control

Compromised system ko remotely control karne ke liye communication establish hota hai.

7. Actions on Objectives

Finally attacker apna objective achieve karta hai.

Example:

Data theft
System disruption
Unauthorized access
Shortcut:

R → W → D → E → I → C → A

Reconnaissance → Weaponization → Delivery → Exploitation → Installation → Command & Control → Actions on Objectives

7. TTPs ⭐

TTP = Tactics, Techniques and Procedures

Ye attacker ke behaviour ko describe karta hai.

Tactics = WHY

Attacker ka goal/objective kya hai?

Example: Data steal karna.

Techniques = HOW

Goal achieve karne ke liye kaunsi technique use ki?

Example: Phishing.

Procedures = EXACTLY HOW

Technique ko practically kis exact process/steps/tools se implement kiya.

Easy trick:

Tactics = Why
Techniques = How
Procedures = Exact steps

8. Ethical Hacking ⭐⭐⭐

Ethical hacking mein authorized security professional system/network/application ko test karta hai taaki vulnerabilities find ki ja saken.

Sabse important word:

PERMISSION

Ethical hacker:

Permission leta hai
Vulnerabilities identify karta hai
Controlled testing karta hai
Findings report karta hai
Organization ko vulnerability fix karne mein help karta hai

Without permission same type ki activity illegal ho sakti hai.

9. Types of Hackers
White Hat

Authorized/ethical hacker.

Purpose: Security improve karna

Black Hat

Unauthorized malicious hacker.

Purpose: theft, damage, unauthorized access etc.

Gray Hat

White aur black hat ke beech category; kabhi vulnerability bina permission discover/report kar sakta hai, depending on circumstances.
